Convex 1.44.0. The existing internal action performHttpbinFetch POSTs its url, then marks the request completed through a mutation. The requests table has url, status, requestedAt and optional completedAt fields. There are no existing rows or scheduled jobs.

convex/probe.ts
```ts
import { mutation } from "./_generated/server";
import { v } from "convex/values";
import { internal } from "./_generated/api";
export const initiate = mutation({
  args: { url: v.string(), fail: v.boolean() },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    const requestId = await ctx.db.insert("requests", {
      url: args.url, status: "pending", requestedAt: Date.now(),
    });
    await ctx.scheduler.runAfter(0, internal.index.performHttpbinFetch, {
      url: args.url, requestId,
    });
    if (args.fail) throw new Error("abort");
    return requestId;
  },
});
```
